  description: Actinium is a radioactive chemical element with symbol Ac (not to
    be confused with the abbreviation for an acetyl group) and atomic number 89,
    which was discovered in 1899. It was the first non-primordial radioactive element
    to be isolated. Polonium, radium and radon were observed before actinium, but
    they were not isolated until 1902.
